{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronFibreEmbedding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronFibreEmbedding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.energy","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The embedding energy (from Möbius energy constraint). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.phi","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.theta","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The base point in the projective line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronFibreEmbedding","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L38-L76","doc":"The **data** of a fibre-compatible hadron embedding: a base point, its\npartner coordinate, and the embedding energy, all over `R_q`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:hadron-fibre-embedding}`\n\n**This structure encodes NO conditions, and the docstring now says so.**\nThe four the module header names — integrability, fibre confinement, Hopf\ncompatibility, volume compatibility — are not fields here and never were\nencoded as propositions; a reader who needs one must state it separately\nagainst this data.\n\n**Both universe-`Prop` fields are now gone.** `integrable` was removed\n2026-09-07 as measured-dead. `confined` was KEPT at that time on the\nstated ground that \"it is read by four declarations\" — and that is a\n**name collision**, not a readership. Re-measured 2026-09-14 across the\nLean tree:\n\n- `DownQuark.confined` / `UpQuark.confined` are `Bool` (`= true := rfl`);\n- `ConfinedParticle.confined` and\n  `ConfinementPhaseStratification.confined` are applied to a parameter\n  (`h.confined q`), so they are functions on a different carrier;\n- `confinedNet` is a different name again.\n\nThere is **no** `.confined` projection on a `HadronFibreEmbedding` and\n**no** `confined :=` construction site anywhere, so the field was exactly\nas dead as `integrable`. Same disposition, same evidence, same file.\n\nThe lesson generalises and is the one AGENTS.md records for `markovZ`:\n**a field name is not an identifier — resolve a \"who reads this?\" claim to\nthe declaration, not to the token.** Consumption is not the test in any\ncase; a field typed with the universe `Prop` is chosen by the constructor,\nso reading it constrains nothing even when the reader is genuine. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:hadron-fibre-embedding","label":"def:hadron-fibre-embedding","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-fibre-embedding.lean#L32-L34","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}